<title>UK: Brent crude from chains - two clocked and one kept.</title>
<headline>Brent crude from chains - two clocked and one kept.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Of the three Brent cargoes which turned wet on Tuesday, two were subject to five o'clocking and one was kept, traders said.</p>
<p>Of the three cargoes due to load in the November 13-15 range, one was kept by British Petroleum who was five o'clocked with another, and J.P. Morgan was five o'clocked with the third cargo, traders said.</p>
<p>--Siobhan Hayden, London Newsroom +44 71 542 8978</p>
